  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Deloitte Consulting's federal business has $82.1M in contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Deloitte Consulting has 51 awards so far and an average award size of $1.6M. Deloitte Consulting's obligations fell 97.5% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows larger prior-year totals: FY22 $2.6B, FY23 $2.9B, FY24 $3.3B, FY25 $3B, and FY26 $3.2B. Top buyers for FY2027 to date are the Department of Veterans Affairs with $56.5M and the General Services Administration with $14.4M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $5.1M and the Department of Transportation with $2.5M. Top markets for FY2027 to date are Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services with $51.5M, Computer Systems Design Services with $23.6M, and Engineering Services with $9.6M. The current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year awards.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Deloitte Consulting's federal contracting trended over recent years?",
        "body": "Deloitte Consulting's obligations reached $3.3B in FY24 and stayed at multi-billion-dollar levels through FY26. Deloitte Consulting's obligations for FY2027 to date are $82.1M, and Deloitte Consulting's obligations fell 97.5% year over year. The fiscal-history series runs FY22 $2.6B, FY23 $2.9B, FY24 $3.3B, FY25 $3B, and FY26 $3.2B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Deloitte Consulting's primary federal customers and what markets do they buy?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer for FY2027 to date with $56.5M, followed by the General Services Administration with $14.4M and the Department of Homeland Security with $5.1M. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services is the top market with $51.5M, Computer Systems Design Services is second with $23.6M, and Engineering Services accounts for $9.6M for the current year to date."
      }
    ]
  },
